qemu-guest-agent
# VirtualBox: lets the host resize the guest screen, which VMs default to
# 800x600 or 1024x768 without. The kernel's own vboxguest/vboxsf modules do
# the rest. Harmless on real hardware: the service exits when not in a VM.
virtualbox-guest-utils
# DisplayLink docks. evdi is the kernel module the DisplayLink Manager daemon
# renders through; without it a dock's screens simply never appear. Both are
# vendored from the AUR into pkgs/ -- see docs/repository.md. displaylink is
# proprietary (Synaptics EULA) and is the one non-free package in the image.
#
# evdi is a DKMS module, so dkms and linux-headers have to be here too: the
# module is compiled during the image build, against the `linux` above. That
# costs roughly 600 MB uncompressed (linux-headers 318 MB, gcc 232 MB,
# binutils 45 MB), which zstd squashes down considerably in the squashfs. It
# is worth it because the installer copies this filesystem to disk with
# unpackfs, so DKMS is also what rebuilds evdi on the installed system after
# the user's first kernel update. A prebuilt .ko would die at that point.
evdi-dkms
displaylink
dkms
linux-headers
